# Shell scripts run inside Linux containers (bind-mounted by docker-compose,
# e.g. infra/patroni/*.sh) — a CRLF shebang line fails to exec there. Force
# LF regardless of a contributor's core.autocrlf, which otherwise converts
# to CRLF on checkout on Windows.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Config files read by Linux processes: infra/haproxy/haproxy.cfg is
# bind-mounted into the haproxy container, infra/patroni/patroni.yml is
# COPY'd into the Patroni image.
#
# Unlike the shebang case above, this is consistency rather than a known
# break — haproxy 3.0 was observed parsing a CRLF config without
# complaint, and PyYAML tolerates CRLF by design. But neither of those is
# a guarantee worth depending on across versions, and a file whose only
# job is to be read by a Linux process has no reason to carry Windows
# line endings in the first place.
*.cfg text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
